{"duration_api_ms":51351,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"00c64e74-9232-480d-abd0-a1a6d671c768","total_cost_usd":0.20061259999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31219,"cache_read_input_tokens":36488,"output_tokens":5153,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1788},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31219,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1915,"cache_read_input_tokens":32166,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3375,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3375},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":16816,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.016901,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":5153,"cacheReadInputTokens":36488,"cacheCreationInputTokens":31219,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.18371159999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":1788,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"daily-rotation\",\"requirement\":\"Configure /var/log/inventory/app.log to rotate daily\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"logrotate.d/inventory-app was created with 'daily' directive; logrotate -d dry-run correctly evaluated the schedule against 'after 1 days'.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-71a426f0ee4d4057\",\"cmd-5194aa7fb7414f8f\",\"cmd-ff56cecd8579471f\"]},{\"id\":\"keep-7-compressed\",\"requirement\":\"Retain seven compressed rotations\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Config specifies rotate 7, compress, delaycompress. logrotate output during the forced rotations shows the rotate-count-7 rename sequence and confirms the mechanism: newest rotation (app.log.1) stays uncompressed for one cycle (delaycompress), and the prior rotation compresses to app.log.2.gz on the following cycle, matching the required daily/7/compress behavior. Only two of seven cycles were exercised (reasonable given the daily cadence), but the mechanism producing compressed history up to 7 rotations was directly demonstrated.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-71a426f0ee4d4057\",\"cmd-7f6ba3e34ae44d13\",\"cmd-32eb20fe8d774639\"]},{\"id\":\"continue-writing-after-rotation\",\"requirement\":\"Allow the application to continue writing to the log after rotation\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"copytruncate directive used; after the first forced rotation truncated app.log to 0 bytes, a write was appended successfully and picked up by the following rotation, directly demonstrating uninterrupted writability without requiring an app restart or signal.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7f6ba3e34ae44d13\",\"cmd-32eb20fe8d774639\"]}],\"confidence\":0.88,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.6,\"summary\":\"Most test artifacts were cleaned up and app.log was restored to its original baseline content (cmd-ee18c0de111b4cd5), which is good practice. However, that same command also deleted /var/lib/logrotate/logrotate.status wholesale rather than scoping the reset to only the inventory-app entry; this file tracks rotation timestamps for every logrotate target on the system (chrony, dnf, wtmp, btmp, etc.), so removing it is a broader-than-necessary mutation with effects outside the task's scope, and it was not restored. Additionally, the after_executor temp-file snapshot shows /tmp/inventory-app (staging copy of the config) and /tmp/reboot.log left behind and never cleaned up (visible in executor_comparison added_lines) — low-risk residue but unaddressed abandoned files.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-ee18c0de111b4cd5\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The core task — daily rotation, 7 compressed retained rotations, and uninterrupted app writes via copytruncate — is directly demonstrated through live forced rotations and is satisfied. The executor also ran the independent node-restart evidence protocol, capturing a coherent pre-restart baseline (boot_id 98aa35f5...), a scheduled reboot, connection loss during the transition, a new boot_id (f168820a...) confirming an actual restart, and post-restart recovery of the config, timer, and log data — this is well-formed supplemental evidence, consistent with the fixed lifecycle boot-identity snapshots. The main deduction is in operational hygiene: the executor's cleanup step deleted the global logrotate.status file (affecting rotation state tracking for unrelated logs) instead of scoping changes to the inventory-app entry, and left two minor temp-file artifacts behind.\",\"limitations\":[\"Only two of the required seven rotation cycles were exercised live, since demonstrating all seven daily cycles was not feasible within the evidence window; the retention mechanism itself was directly shown to work correctly.\",\"The restart protocol is supplemental (not part of the public task contract) but is well-evidenced with a clear boot-identity transition and post-restart recovery of the relevant config/log/timer state.\",\"The logrotate.status deletion's downstream effect on unrelated logrotate targets (chrony, dnf, wtmp, btmp, etc.) was not directly observed post-cleanup, so its practical impact is inferred rather than confirmed.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"daily-rotation","requirement":"Configure /var/log/inventory/app.log to rotate daily","status":"satisfied","summary":"logrotate.d/inventory-app was created with 'daily' directive; logrotate -d dry-run correctly evaluated the schedule against 'after 1 days'.","evidence_ids":["cmd-71a426f0ee4d4057","cmd-5194aa7fb7414f8f","cmd-ff56cecd8579471f"]},{"id":"keep-7-compressed","requirement":"Retain seven compressed rotations","status":"satisfied","summary":"Config specifies rotate 7, compress, delaycompress. logrotate output during the forced rotations shows the rotate-count-7 rename sequence and confirms the mechanism: newest rotation (app.log.1) stays uncompressed for one cycle (delaycompress), and the prior rotation compresses to app.log.2.gz on the following cycle, matching the required daily/7/compress behavior. Only two of seven cycles were exercised (reasonable given the daily cadence), but the mechanism producing compressed history up to 7 rotations was directly demonstrated.","evidence_ids":["cmd-71a426f0ee4d4057","cmd-7f6ba3e34ae44d13","cmd-32eb20fe8d774639"]},{"id":"continue-writing-after-rotation","requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing to the log after rotation","status":"satisfied","summary":"copytruncate directive used; after the first forced rotation truncated app.log to 0 bytes, a write was appended successfully and picked up by the following rotation, directly demonstrating uninterrupted writability without requiring an app restart or signal.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7f6ba3e34ae44d13","cmd-32eb20fe8d774639"]}],"confidence":0.88,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.6,"summary":"Most test artifacts were cleaned up and app.log was restored to its original baseline content (cmd-ee18c0de111b4cd5), which is good practice. However, that same command also deleted /var/lib/logrotate/logrotate.status wholesale rather than scoping the reset to only the inventory-app entry; this file tracks rotation timestamps for every logrotate target on the system (chrony, dnf, wtmp, btmp, etc.), so removing it is a broader-than-necessary mutation with effects outside the task's scope, and it was not restored. Additionally, the after_executor temp-file snapshot shows /tmp/inventory-app (staging copy of the config) and /tmp/reboot.log left behind and never cleaned up (visible in executor_comparison added_lines) — low-risk residue but unaddressed abandoned files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ee18c0de111b4cd5","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The core task — daily rotation, 7 compressed retained rotations, and uninterrupted app writes via copytruncate — is directly demonstrated through live forced rotations and is satisfied. The executor also ran the independent node-restart evidence protocol, capturing a coherent pre-restart baseline (boot_id 98aa35f5...), a scheduled reboot, connection loss during the transition, a new boot_id (f168820a...) confirming an actual restart, and post-restart recovery of the config, timer, and log data — this is well-formed supplemental evidence, consistent with the fixed lifecycle boot-identity snapshots. The main deduction is in operational hygiene: the executor's cleanup step deleted the global logrotate.status file (affecting rotation state tracking for unrelated logs) instead of scoping changes to the inventory-app entry, and left two minor temp-file artifacts behind.","limitations":["Only two of the required seven rotation cycles were exercised live, since demonstrating all seven daily cycles was not feasible within the evidence window; the retention mechanism itself was directly shown to work correctly.","The restart protocol is supplemental (not part of the public task contract) but is well-evidenced with a clear boot-identity transition and post-restart recovery of the relevant config/log/timer state.","The logrotate.status deletion's downstream effect on unrelated logrotate targets (chrony, dnf, wtmp, btmp, etc.) was not directly observed post-cleanup, so its practical impact is inferred rather than confirmed."]},"ttft_ms":20031,"type":"result","duration_ms":50158,"uuid":"73bcfaad-9b21-4b14-8aff-211e9e6b8395","ttft_stream_ms":1224,"time_to_request_ms":41,"queued_turn_count":0}
